WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.875
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Wednesday, October twenty first.

2
00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:15.539
Five minutes on the last twenty four hours of security developments, from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

3
00:00:15.539 --> 00:00:19.394
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:19.394 --> 00:00:20.362
Our top story is Sudan.

5
00:00:20.362 --> 00:00:29.492
BBC Africa reports that Sudan's army is accused of several drone strikes that reportedly killed more than two hundred people, including dozens travelling to a funeral.

6
00:00:29.492 --> 00:00:33.449
That toll has not been independently confirmed.

7
00:00:33.449 --> 00:00:38.082
Next, updates on stories we covered yesterday.

8
00:00:38.082 --> 00:00:44.931
Update on the Ebola outbreak: BBC Africa reports Kenya has now confirmed nine cases, all linked to one traveler from Congo.

9
00:00:44.931 --> 00:00:52.045
Update on Saudi Arabia: the UK Foreign Office says King Khalid Airport in Riyadh continues to be targeted.

10
00:00:52.045 --> 00:00:59.247
Update on northern Ethiopia: the UN humanitarian office, OCHA, says renewed fighting is compounding an already dire humanitarian situation.

11
00:00:59.247 --> 00:01:05.953
Update on Italy: the UK Foreign Office has added a national strike planned for October thirtieth.

12
00:01:05.953 --> 00:01:16.420
Also new, Radio Free Europe reports that Russia has freed Stephen Hubbard, a U.S. schoolteacher held since twenty twenty two, in what is being framed as a goodwill gesture.

13
00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:22.660
And Global Affairs Canada is tracking Typhoon Champi, expected to sweep across Okinawa and Japan's Ryukyu Islands.

14
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.908
Now a few quick notes by region.

15
00:01:26.908 --> 00:01:42.961
In the Middle East, the Institute for the Study of War says Houthi and Yemeni government aligned forces are still contesting high ground over western Taiz, and that the Houthis likely fired ballistic missiles at Marib City on October nineteenth.

16
00:01:42.961 --> 00:01:49.490
In South Asia, Radio Free Europe reports rising militant attacks along the Iran Pakistan border.

17
00:01:49.490 --> 00:02:00.673
TRAC reports militants killed a Pakistani soldier in Charsadda, and that three suspected Kuki National Front militants were arrested after a deadly attack on civilians in Manipur, India.

18
00:02:00.673 --> 00:02:10.960
In Africa, BBC Africa reports residents near Pretoria, South Africa, were told not to drink or cook with tap water after more than four hundred people fell ill.

19
00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:18.865
ACLED reports vigilante mob violence in Kenya, centered on Nairobi but recorded in forty six counties this year.

20
00:02:18.865 --> 00:02:28.847
In Latin America, InSight Crime reports five alleged Chapitos members were arrested in Mexico, and TRAC reports four public officials in Taxco, Guerrero, were arrested over cartel links.

21
00:02:28.847 --> 00:02:34.655
TRAC also reports Colombian forces seized explosives meant for drone attacks in Buenaventura.

22
00:02:34.655 --> 00:02:47.673
In Europe, TRAC reports a Gen Z protest movement is calling for nationwide demonstrations in Germany on October thirty first, and two suspected Islamic State linked jihadists were arrested in Catalonia, Spain.

23
00:02:47.673 --> 00:02:57.654
On cyber, The Record reports California officials warned millions of students about a data breach at a testing service contractor.

24
00:02:57.654 --> 00:02:59.111
That's today's brief.

25
00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:07.389
It summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

26
00:03:07.389 --> 00:03:09.656
This brief is digitally narrated.

27
00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:10.622
Questions?

28
00:03:10.622 --> 00:03:14.144
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

29
00:03:14.144 --> 00:03:16.469
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
